    "title": "Police searching for missing person in Michigan - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ohio Statewide Staff ,\n3 hours ago MICHIGAN — The Kent County Sheriff’s Office is asking for the public’s help in locating a missing 28-year-old man.\nDeputies issued a missing persons alert Wednesday evening for Toby Ross, who was last seen leaving the area of 68th Street and Division Street in Gaines Township.\nRoss is described as being approximately 5 feet 9 inches tall, weighing around 160 pounds, with black hair and hazel eyes.\nAccording to authorities, he was last seen wearing a brown hoodie, black jeans, a black backpack and brown boots. Investigators said Ross did not have a vehicle or cellphone with him at the time of his disappearance.\nAnyone with information on his whereabouts is urged to contact law enforcement immediately.\nThe post Police searching for missing person in Michigan first appeared on Ohio Statewide .",
    "summary": "By Ohio Statewide Staff , 1 hours ago MICHIGAN — The Kent County Sheriff’s Office is asking for the public’s help in locating a missing 28-year-old man. Deputies issued a missing persons alert Wednesday evening for Toby Ross, who was last seen leaving the area of 68th Street and Division Street in Gaines Township. Ross is described as being approximately 5 feet 9 inches tall, weighing around 160 pounds, with black hair and hazel eyes. Anyone with information on his whereabouts is urged to contact law enforcement immediately.",
